index 0000000..f5792d6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/experiments/hot_cache/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,91 @@
+# Bounded foreground-cache restart feasibility probe
+
+This isolated experiment changes no service defaults or packaged JNI. Its native
+base is `cc8367a1076b6245574f209c7d007118cf9016b1`. `build.sh` enforces the matching
+qualified runtime SHA256
+`18d5865e39cccede36d63146eb9037837b423199930504e3730d2d91d9ff6214` before copying or
+linking `librocksdbjni-linux64.so`. The image's older standalone librocksdb was
+ABI incompatible and was rejected. The image is only a compiler container.
+
+Run `build.sh SOURCE CANDIDATE OUTPUT` inside
+`codex-paired-compaction-qualified-build-cache:20261011`, with at most 3 CPUs and
+8 GiB, then `python3 test.py OUTPUT/probe OUTPUT`. `probe.h` exposes a synchronous
+C ABI for Java 25 FFM; one call owns all C++ objects and the caller supplies an
+output buffer of at least 2048 bytes. Calls sharing paths must be serialized.
+Mode 0 atomically creates an absent fixture directory and an exact format/base/runtime
+marker. Other modes require a real directory and a regular non-symlink marker
+before DB::Open; its generation marker is then verified before replacement writes.
+Canonical snapshot destinations must be outside the DB directory, including
+symlink aliases, preventing accidental SST/manifest overwrites. Mode 3 changes values,
+flushes and compacts both CFs, exercising SST identity replacement.
+
+The fixture uses a 16 MiB HyperClock cache for DATA and METADATA. Values uniquely
+encode CF, key and generation, so wrong-block reuse cannot pass equality checks.
+Only capture modes (0/2) install the observer. Read/replacement modes (1/3) use
+the primary cache directly, without observer locks or registry allocations;
+`capture_observer_attached` makes this branch explicit in the report.
+Only Insert/Lookup performed within synchronous foreground Gets qualifies for
+the bounded 4096-key latest-observation registry. Transparent string-view lookup
+and list splicing reuse existing nodes/strings on repeated hits. The same
+transparent hash lets secondary-cache misses look up borrowed key bytes without
+allocating a temporary string. Startup/build/compaction
+activity is excluded. The fixture disables metadata pinning and deliberately
+erases unreferenced primary entries before Gets, then force-erases every bounded
+snapshot key and verifies primary-only lookup misses. HCC
+`EraseUnRefEntries` is best effort (single CAS per slot), which initially allowed
+a filter to survive and made one strict restore test fail. This cold-primary boundary
+proves DATA, INDEX and FILTER restoration within actual foreground Gets,
+independently of Open's eager metadata loads. `unscoped_hits` reports every secondary hit outside the scoped bulk Gets,
+including Open, generation-marker reads and fixture compaction.
+This is a mechanism test, not a model of production pinning or cache warmth.
+
+Capture obtains primary-only handles for observed keys, filters stable SST
+prefixes from every live CF, verifies helper/deleter identity, serializes supported
+resident blocks, and releases each handle before disk writes. Basic helpers on
+previously restored blocks are recovered by role. Per-CF DATA/INDEX/FILTER
+captures and hits establish both CFs' coverage in this fixture. The SSD snapshot
+retains only offsets/keys in its RAM index; payloads are read on demand. Serialized
+primary objects require `kVolatileTier` source in `cache/typed_cache.h`, regardless
+of physical SSD placement. Missing, empty or rejected snapshots install no
+secondary adapter and cause zero secondary lookup attempts.
+
+Format v2 is explicitly little-endian x86-64, with an 84-byte header containing
+magic, version, count, exact native runtime SHA256 and header CRC32C. Each record
+has bounded lengths and CRC32C over lengths, role, key and value. Validate the
+whole generation before activation; recheck records before deserialization.
+Files are capped at 64 MiB, blocks at 1 MiB, records at 4096. Capture reserves at
+most the byte cap for its generation plus at most one block-sized serialization
+buffer, alongside bounded registry/index storage. Restore holds at most one
+block-sized validation buffer plus its bounded index. The fixture's SST-property
+inventory is small; no production bound on that inventory is established.
+
+Restore and capture use five-second cooperative deadlines checked between I/O
+and records; the tests exercise expiry. A blocking syscall/fsync is not forcibly
+interrupted, so this is not a hard wall-clock or I/O-rate guarantee. Capture
+writes a unique temporary, fsyncs it, renames atomically, then fsyncs the directory.
+`publication_state` distinguishes `durable`, `not_requested`, and
+`published_durability_uncertain`: rename can install a complete new generation
+before directory fsync fails. Only pre-rename errors preserve the previous file.
+Fixed output formatting cannot allocate after publication. Fault tests use
+`RSHC_TEST_FAIL_BEFORE_RENAME`, `RSHC_TEST_FAIL_AFTER_RENAME`,
+`RSHC_TEST_EXPIRE_CAPTURE`, and `RSHC_TEST_EXPIRE_RESTORE`. Stale temporary names do
+not block a later capture; hard crashes can still leave owned temporaries.
+
+Observed mechanism: 2048 verified Gets per process, with 488 foreground restored
+blocks: 242 DATA + 1 INDEX + 1 FILTER in each CF. The 2,006,353-byte generation
+survives restart, recapture and another restart. After replacing SSTs and changing
+values, the old snapshot has zero foreground hits; new snapshots restore the new
+values. Strict tests reject crashes as expected failures and cover malformed
+headers/records, checksum/version/runtime mismatch, duplicate keys, truncation,
+FIFO inputs, byte limits, absent snapshots, expiry and publication states.
+IO_uring is unavailable in Docker and falls back to POSIX.
+
+Limits: no HDD latency/throughput result, production wiring, pinned-metadata
+hotness observation, separate DATA/METADATA quota, time-adaptive admission,
+asynchronous Get/MultiGet coverage, background concurrency stress or hard syscall
+cancellation. Ambiguous OtherBlock roles, including dictionaries, are excluded.
+Capture buffers a bounded generation in RAM; startup scans its payload to validate
+before retaining the index. Exact-runtime compatibility is intentionally strict;
+upgrading native builds currently discards snapshots. CRC detects corruption,
+not adversarial tampering. Scoped retention/cleanup of crash temporaries remains
+future work. Generic operational exceptions do not imply a publication state.
diff --git a/experiments/hot_cache/build.sh b/experiments/hot_cache/build.sh
new file mode 100755
index 0000000..675eea9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/experiments/hot_cache/build.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env bash
+set -euo pipefail
+# Run in qualified Docker image with <=3 CPUs/8GiB. Source is exact cc8367a
+# experiment checkout, runtime is the already-qualified cc8367a native artifact.
+source_root=${1:?source checkout}
+candidate=${2:?exact native candidate directory}
+output=${3:?owned output directory}
+expected_runtime=18d5865e39cccede36d63146eb9037837b423199930504e3730d2d91d9ff6214
+actual_runtime=$(sha256sum "$candidate/librocksdbjni-linux64.so" | cut -d' ' -f1)
+if [[ "$actual_runtime" != "$expected_runtime" ]]; then
+  echo "Rejecting incompatible runtime: $actual_runtime" >&2
+  exit 1
+fi
+mkdir -p "$output"
+cp "$candidate/librocksdbjni-linux64.so" "$output/"
+flags=(-std=c++20 -O1 -g -DROCKSDB_PLATFORM_POSIX -DROCKSDB_LIB_IO_POSIX -DROCKSDB_USE_RTTI -I"$source_root" -I"$source_root/include")
+g++-12 "${flags[@]}" -fPIC -shared "$source_root/experiments/hot_cache/probe.cc" -L"$output" -lrocksdbjni-linux64 '-Wl,-rpath,$ORIGIN' -o "$output/libhot_cache_probe.so"
+g++-12 "${flags[@]}" -DRSHC_MAIN "$source_root/experiments/hot_cache/probe.cc" -L"$output" -lrocksdbjni-linux64 '-Wl,-rpath,$ORIGIN' -o "$output/probe"
+sha256sum "$output/librocksdbjni-linux64.so" "$output/libhot_cache_probe.so"
